+## Experimental H2 source-driven plate
+
+When the user explicitly requests the H2 FSGen-to-native plate workflow, use
+`experimental_h2_create_plate` with an absolute local `.fs` path, the exact
+workspace Part Studio URL, and its connected editor tab ID. The same Python
+environment that launches this MCP server must have `h2cad` and its pinned FSGen
+dependency installed. The paired bridge config must pin the H2 SQLite journal
+and the explicitly approved empty test target. The tool delegates once to the
+existing H2 CLI, which validates geometry locally, journals each possible
+native write, and reads back the resulting definitions. It does not use REST
+for CAD writes or silently switch to a different target. This path currently
+supports one Top rectangle and one blind extrusion; unsupported source features
+fail before modeling. Do not use it on an existing collaborative Part Studio.
+
+The result `h2_command_completed` reports H2 definition checks only. Independently
+verify saved solid geometry and human editability. If the tool returns
+`needs_readback`, inspect the pinned journal and exact editor state; never invoke
+the tool again on that target until the uncertain operation is reconciled.
+
